// Pinned decree figures: 22-day monthly cap, SMIC formula and 2021 BMAF
// rates, half-day and part-time amounts, computed complement threshold,
// job-seeker flat 22 (D. 544-4/6/7/8).
//
// D. 544-4 pins the monthly maximum at 22: the decree rule derives the
// same within-limit head without a retained-max input. D. 544-6 builds
// the daily rate from 2022 by the single formula A = (7*shn)/(1-a),
// rounded to the cent (non-tie outputs are source-derived as
// mode-indistinguishable; exact half-cent ties are case-flagged and
// stay pending per D75, B-PFAJPP-TIE-ARRONDI; the division exactness
// is qualified by the deferred run, B-PFAJPP-FORMULE-DIVISION),
// halves it for half-days outside L. 5421-1,
// and prices part-time months on the days not worked; the 2021 window
// builds the BMAF percentage rates (10.63 / 12.63 / 5.315 / 6.315 %).
// D. 544-7 builds the 27.19 % threshold and amount from the retained
// BMAF; the decree threshold test is «supérieures ou égales» where the
// L. 544-7 rule reads strict «supérieures» — the decree governs the
// threshold it sets (proposed reading, journal). D. 544-8 checks the
// job-seeker flat days against the decree 22 outside the
// occasional-activity exception, which ends at the L. 544-1 boundary.
// F05-01: decree monthly amounts gate on the month conformity (daily
// 22 or flat 22) plus the qualified envelope, except demi-day and
// part-time amounts, which gate on the envelope only (monthly
// conversion boundary B-PFAJPP-DEMI-PLAFOND).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.ajpp version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-ajpp";

